    'Vol. 1, ch. 1 (p. 4): "How many generations of Blacks have believed that they are cursed and inferior to the rest of mankind because of the so-called curse of Ham, a corrupted teaching of the Bible that has been traditionally propounded by certain Christians?" Part Two, Disproving Racist Lies (pp. 139-150): "God never cursed Ham at all. Noah did the cursing — but it was not Ham he cursed, it was Ham’s son Canaan. And Noah is not God"; "God does not curse anyone through all eternity"; the shade argument ("then what shade of black would they be?"); Galatians 3:13 and the Law: "If, as the Bible says, I am redeemed from the curse of the law through Christ, then, if blackness is a curse, the blackness of my skin ought to vanish and I ought to be another color."',
